# shellcheck global config — debian-bootc
# See: https://github.com/koalaman/shellcheck/wiki/Ignore
#
# Per-script disables use inline `# shellcheck disable=SCxxxx` with a comment
# explaining why (see docs/coding-rules.md § Shell).  Global disables here are
# only for rules that would fire correctly but are inapplicable to the whole
# project.

# SC2250: Prefer putting braces around variable references — the project
# already uses "${VAR}" everywhere; the rule fires on $? and $# in safe
# contexts.  Suppressed globally; violations in new code are caught by review.
disable=SC2250
